MT6895 VCP review regression checks
=================================

Run make run_tests in this directory on the build host (Python 3, Clang or
GCC, Linux V4L2 UAPI headers, pthreads and address/undefined sanitizers
required). The scripts extract actual driver C functions and tables.

The layout oracle independently packs row-major MSBs and column-major
low-bit pairs. It exercises all ten bits rather than accepting a +/-3
threshold. The ownership test races both owners and covers re-entry,
retained cleanup and externally running firmware.

The capture test checks MM21 byte layout across strides, partial tile rows
and unaligned views, format minimum/step bounds, and DMA-BUF CPU-access
pairing, acquisition rollback and release failures across multiple planes.

test_bitstream.py exercises the actual OUTPUT buffer_prepare and submit_source
paths with an exporter shim that makes producer data visible only on begin
and changes the mapping on end. It checks begin/end errors, missing mappings,
MMAP snapshot revalidation, MPEG4 visual-object/sequence-end dispatch and AV1
extension/length boundaries through both guards. The small framing vectors
do not claim full codec conformance.

test_headers.py runs the actual header parser, event collector and worker
with synchronous and delayed firmware release events. Repeated incomplete
headers, stop/resume (including release coincident with stop), timeouts,
watchdog errors and incorrect cookies must preserve the pending buffer and
prevent a second submission until the first input has been released. These
are deterministic host fault injections, not firmware execution.

test_encoder_caps.py exercises ENUM_FMT, TRY_FMT and S_FMT using each of the
seven platform data entries and all nine raw input formats. Unsupported
legacy formats must negotiate back to NV12M. It also checks the actual
HEADER_MODE registration expression for both backends. The geometry and
control-framework shims do not replace encoding or control ioctl tests on
the corresponding SoCs.

On the phone, build ownership_probe.c with -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror,
then run under a 30-second timeout with encoder and decoder device paths.
It verifies early decoder reservations, both codec startup orders,
same-handle retry and ten simultaneous starts. It does not queue frames.
Full decode/encode tests must separately check pixels, per-picture PTS,
drain, DRC, fault cleanup and the current module/kernel build identity.
